  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Those tiny dashed lines on the highway are much bigger than your brain thinks.",
      "start": 0.04,
      "end": 3.918
    },
    {
      "text": "In the United States, a standard broken lane marking is typically about 10 feet",
      "start": 4.214,
      "end": 8.535
    },
    {
      "text": "long,",
      "start": 8.535,
      "end": 8.803
    },
    {
      "text": "and the gap after it is around 30 feet.",
      "start": 9.095,
      "end": 11.132
    },
    {
      "text": "But from inside a moving car, perspective makes them look like tiny little strips of",
      "start": 11.407,
      "end": 15.497
    },
    {
      "text": "paint.",
      "start": 15.497,
      "end": 15.819
    },
    {
      "text": "10 feet is about 3 meters, so if Bill stood next to one of those little road",
      "start": 16.138,
      "end": 20.354
    },
    {
      "text": "lines,",
      "start": 20.354,
      "end": 20.676
    },
    {
      "text": "the line would absolutely destroy him in a height comparison.",
      "start": 20.955,
      "end": 23.654
    },
    {
      "text": "Your brain has basically been shrinking the road underneath you this entire time.",
      "start": 23.998,
      "end": 27.535
    }
  ],
